## github-connect

Connect a GitHub repository + branch to a project, deploy the branch's current HEAD, then automatically deploy every future push through the same pipeline as `somewhere deploy`.

Preferred path: `github_app_install` if needed, then an ID from `github_installations`, passed as `installation_id`. The App uses short-lived tokens and signed App-level webhooks—no PAT paste or manual repo webhook. By default this call resolves and deploys HEAD immediately; `github_status` reports the returned `initial_deploy.commit_sha` as deployed or failed. The PAT/manual-webhook fields remain compatibility fallbacks.

**Example:**

Example transcript or fragment

```text
{ "project_id": "my-saas", "repo": "alice/my-saas", "installation_id": 123, "branch": "main" }
// Returns: { "repo": "alice/my-saas", "via_app": true, "initial_deploy": { "status": "deploying", "commit_sha": "..." } }
```

## github-status

Show a project's GitHub push-to-deploy connection: repo, branch, App/manual mode, and the last exact commit's deploy status/error. After `github_connect`, it reports that commit as `deployed` or `failed`; `connected` only means the repo is linked; that commit's own status says whether it deployed. Returns `{ connected: false }` if no repo is connected.

**Example:**

Example transcript or fragment

```text
{ "project_id": "my-saas" }
// Returns: { "connected": true, "repo": "alice/my-saas", "branch": "main", "hook_installed": true, "last_commit_sha": "...", "last_status": "deployed" }
```

## github-disconnect

Disconnect a project from GitHub push-to-deploy. Removes the connection and best-effort deletes a per-repository webhook when present. Already-deployed code stays live—this only stops future pushes from auto-deploying.

**Example:**

Example transcript or fragment

```text
{ "project_id": "my-saas" }
// Returns: { "disconnected": true }
```

## github-list-repos

List repositories available to a GitHub App installation so you can pick one for `github_connect`. Preferred: pass `installation_id` from `github_installations`. A personal access token remains an optional compatibility fallback and is used only for this request.

**Example:**

Example transcript or fragment

```text
{ "installation_id": 123 }
// Returns: [{ "name": "alice/my-saas", "private": false, "default_branch": "main", ... }]
```

